@startuml
title Archive Search Workbench - architecture (generic)\nRuns on any single host; other machines can contribute drives optionally
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

package "App host (any machine: laptop, server, or NAS)" as host {
 rectangle "Flask web app\nweb_app.py - port 5059\n(mono-file, embedded HTML/CSS/JS)" as app
 database "SQLite catalog\narchive_catalog.db\n(searchable offline)" as db
 folder "Recoll index\n(full-text engine)" as recoll
 folder "Config\nconfig/config.yaml" as config
 rectangle "Read-only mount\nmount_readonly.sh (ntfs-3g)" as mnt
}

package "External archive media\n(USB HDD / SSD / stick / SD card)" as media {
 rectangle "Labelled drives\nARCHIVE-DISK-XXX\n(mounted READ-ONLY)" as disks
}

rectangle "Browser\n(user, LAN)" as browser
rectangle "Donations\n(external, see NOTICE)" as donate

browser --> app : HTTP :5059 (search, manage)
app --> browser : HTML / JSON
app --> db : read / write metadata
app --> recoll : full-text search
app --> config : read settings
disks --> mnt : attach read-only
mnt --> app : scan & index
browser --> donate : donate click (new tab)

note bottom of app
Single-machine is the base case: plug a drive
into the app host, register, scan, index, search.
No always-on central server is required.
end note

note right of disks
Read-only is sacred: mount -o ro via ntfs-3g.
Sticker on the medium = UUID link in the catalog.
Search keeps working after the drive is removed.
end note

' --- Optional: drives on other machines via USB/IP ---
package "Optional: another machine on the LAN" as remote #line.dashed {
 rectangle "Drive plugged in here\n+ USB/IP exporter (port 3240)\n+ per-machine agent (port 5060)" as rexp
}
rexp ..> app : USB/IP + agent (see network-usb/)

note bottom of remote
Optional distributed mode: attach a drive to ANY
machine on your network; the app host imports it
over USB/IP and indexes it as if it were local.
end note

@enduml
